---
import BaseLayout from "../../components/BaseLayout.astro";
import { projects } from "../../data/projects";

const project = projects[1];
---
<BaseLayout title="Ink" description={project.description} work={{ type: "CreativeWork" }}>
  <header class="page-hero container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Project / Operator workflow</p>
    <h1>Ink</h1>
    <a class="text-link" href="/projects/">← All projects</a>
    <p class="lead">A local credential notebook for recording where identities were discovered, what was validated, and which observations need follow-up.</p>
  </header>
  <section class="container section content-layout">
    <figure class="project-flow">
      <ol><li>Record the identity and source</li><li>Attach validation notes</li><li>Review observations by user</li><li>Export the notebook for private review</li></ol>
      <figcaption>Ink’s notebook workflow.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The problem</h2>
      <p>When observations are spread across terminal history and ad hoc notes, it is easy to lose the source of a credential or the context in which it was validated.</p>
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>A Python CLI stores user records, credentials, and notes in a per-notebook SQLite database. Records can be listed and edited, and observations from different hosts or services can be attached to the relevant user.</p>
      <h2>Review and export</h2>
      <p>Ink is a private project. It exports a notebook to HTML for offline review, so the notes and validation history are available during report preparation.</p>
      <h2>Example record</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt>Identity</dt><dd>sample.reader</dd>
        <dt>Source</dt><dd>Fictional assessment notes</dd>
        <dt>Validation</dt><dd>Read access verified on the sample service</dd>
        <dt>Reuse</dt><dd>Pending review</dd>
      </dl>
      <div class="tag-list">{project.stack.map((tag) => <span class="tag">{tag}</span>)}</div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
